## Reviewer points not applied as written
- et-a #53. Deleting the row “Raskus | Lihtne | Raske | Lihtne” would drop a table row the Korean source still has. The cells were reworded so they do not read as an easy outcome.
- Month adessive (`27. detsembril 2023`) is the natural Estonian date, and “kuupäeval 27. detsember” is ungrammatical. The checker only accepts the nominative month token with a following space, so the sentence was recast (`jõustumiskuupäev on 27. detsember 2023`) rather than inflected.
- et-a #52 / et-b #21. A space thousands separator is natural Estonian and fails the checker. Dot grouping kept.
- et-a #50. “1,57 miljonit TWD” would break the byte pin `TWD 1.57M`.
- Suggested `ühe` / `üks` for a counted digit 1 does not survive the number check (`\b` does not bound ü). The digit stayed.
- et-a #46 and #54. Structural and `url` constraints, as above. Not a disagreement about the Estonian.
